  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41699672",
      "title": "About the NextJS Pages Router",
      "sourceHash": "02eeab7e980905ee58f0f9b5b854cdba3b3ab54d36358ca435eb137575bdcd86",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.78,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "So at this point, you learned a lot about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "working with NextJS and how you can use NextJS to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 11.733,
          "en": "full stack web applications with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.78,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "Now, if you are visiting the official NextJS documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 20.1,
          "en": "you might notice though that there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.1,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "they're also mentioning an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 26.583,
          "en": "router you can use when working with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 31.59,
          "en": "In this section thus far, we used the so-called App Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.59,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "which is the more modern and recommended way of building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "NextJS apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 39.93,
          "en": "But there also is a Pages Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.93,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "which is essentially an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 47.31,
          "en": "of building NextJS apps, which was the only way in the past,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "and which, at least at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "where I'm recording this, in some regards still is the more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "stable approach, at least in my experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 59.28,
          "en": "Nonetheless, the App Router is the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.28,
          "end": 63.75,
          "en": "but this Pages Router approach definitely has its merits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.75,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "You also might be working on a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 68.52,
          "en": "that's still using this Pages Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.52,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "Now, this Pages Router approach here is simply a different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 76.23,
          "en": "way of building NextJS projects or applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 79.62,
          "en": "but you will still be building full stack applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.62,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "and you will still be using ReactJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 86.73,
          "en": "You'll just be working with a different folder structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "and you'll be using some other features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 93.50999999999999,
          "en": "Now, in the official documentation, you can actually switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.50999999999999,
          "end": 96.21000000000001,
          "en": "between two versions of that documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 99.81,
          "en": "so that you can also learn all about NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.81,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "based on this Pages Router approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "if you prefer using that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "As mentioned, it was the only way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 109.28999999999999,
          "en": "of building NextJS applications in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.28999999999999,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "And speaking of the past, I did record this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 118.5,
          "en": "this NextJS essentials section here in the past already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.5,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "when this Pages Router was the only way of building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 127.07,
          "en": "Next applications, and I decided to keep this old content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 130.56,
          "en": "around because it's still absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.56,
          "end": 134.82,
          "en": "Using this Pages Router is still an absolutely fine way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.82,
          "end": 137.61,
          "en": "of working with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "even though the App Router is the more modern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 141.06,
          "en": "and recommended way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.06,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "But for the reasons I mentioned, stability, older projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "that might still be using the Pages Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "you might still want to learn about the Pages Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 154.23,
          "en": "That's why for the rest of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.23,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "you will find lectures where I again teach you NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "but now using this Pages Router instead of the App Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 165.09,
          "en": "And you can of course skip those lectures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.09,
          "end": 168.15,
          "en": "if you're not interested, but you might want to take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.15,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "at them to learn all about these different versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 173.643,
          "en": "of building NextJS applications.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}